      "problem": "Mike purchased an $80$'s baseball card for $$50.$ If the value of the card increases by $8%$ each year, what expression gives the card's value after $10$ years?",
      "worked_solution": "The card's value is $$50$, and this number increases by $8%$ each year.\n\n$8%$ as a decimal is $0.08.$ Therefore, an increase of $8%$ corresponds to multiplication by a factor of\n\n$$\n1+0.08=1.08.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have:\n\n- After $1$ year, the value of the card is $50\\cdot (1.08)$ dollars.\n\n- After $2$ years, the value of the card is $50\\cdot (1.08)^{2}$ dollars.\n\n- After $3$ years, the value of the card is $50\\cdot (1.08)^{3}$ dollars.\n\n$\\,⋮$\n\n- After $10$ years, the value of the card is $50\\cdot (1.08)^{10}$ dollars.",
